From a4a61b591950650195d24a46fefb27ccf3359369 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 01:35:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] DAG viewer: fix scroll-hijack, size panels to content,
 correct the count

Three fixes to the shared viewer, so a populated DAG (Electronics today,
Embedded once its blockers land) is navigable, not just Embedded's empty
state:

- Mouse wheel no longer zooms and traps the page. Plain wheel scrolls as
  usual; zoom now needs Ctrl (or Cmd), which is also how a trackpad pinch
  arrives. Without this, a viewer stuck on the first chain never scrolled
  down to the others or to the inventory.
- Each chain's panel is sized to the chain (clamp 11rem..70vh by node
  count) instead of a flat 70vh. Seven small two-node chains no longer take
  five screens and bury the inventory beneath them.
- The graph caption counts only this team's epics, not the external
  other-tracker nodes, so it reads "9 of 15" not "16 of 15", and names
  where the unconnected epics are: the inventory below.

Regenerated all three DAG viewers from the changed generator.
